It was raining heavily outside.
The door of the café opened.
I stood behind the counter.
My first customer came inside.
I was a little nervous.
I welcomed him with a smile.
"Namaskaram."
"What would you like?"
I asked.
"I need a cappuccino," he said.
I took that order carefully.
I am learning to converse well with customers.
I made the coffee quickly in the machine.
I had practiced it with Jessy.
It was my second good coffee today.
I poured the coffee into a large cup.
I did not make him wait at all.
"Here is your coffee," I said and handed over the cup.
He gave eighty rupees.
"Thank you," he said smiling.
He went to a table.
My hands were still shaking a little.
